BusinessRule How a row becomes an amount
Description The three styles, and what each does with the numbers it finds.
Examples: CsvAmount
| AmountStyle  | OutwardSign | AmountCell | DebitCell | CreditCell | Amount   | Notes                      |
| Signed       | Negative    | -45.00     |           |            | -45.00   | Taken as written           |
| Signed       | Negative    | 3000.00    |           |            | 3000.00  |                            |
| Signed       | Positive    | 45.00      |           |            | -45.00   | Turned round               |
| Signed       | Positive    | -3000.00   |           |            | 3000.00  |                            |
| DebitCredit  | Negative    |            | 45.00     |            | -45.00   | Debit is always money out  |
| DebitCredit  | Negative    |            |           | 3000.00    | 3000.00  | Credit is always money in  |
| DebitCredit  | Negative    |            | -45.00    |            | -45.00   | A signed debit is still out |
| SignedPaired | Negative    |            | -45.00    | 0.00       | -45.00   | The two are added          |
| SignedPaired | Negative    |            | 0.00      | 3000.00    | 3000.00  |                            |

Attributes CsvAmount
| Attribute   | Type        | Default  |
| AmountStyle | AmountStyle | Signed   |
| OutwardSign | OutwardSign | Negative |
| AmountCell  | String      | none     |
| DebitCell   | String      | none     |
| CreditCell  | String      | none     |
| Amount      | Money       | 0.00     |
| Notes       | String      | none     |

