# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whether a CSV import clears what it brings in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

BusinessRule A book may say not to clear what a CSV import brings in
Description A CSV file from a bank is a statement in everything but name, so
\ what it carries arrives cleared, the same as an OFX download. A CSV
\ file is also what a spreadsheet of one's own looks like, and that is
\ not a statement at all. The book says which kind it gets.
Details Written positively -- the option is whether to clear, defaulting to
\ true -- because a setting whose name contains a negative is read
\ wrongly by somebody eventually. The author's own words for it were
\ "do not set cleared flag on CSV import", which is this option off.
\
\ Only a CSV import asks. An OFX file states a ledger balance and a
\ cleared status of its own, so there is nothing for a book-wide
\ option to decide there, and a transaction typed into a register is
\ uncleared whatever the book says.
\
\ Stored on the book's own row, beside the fiscal year start and the
\ check window, so it travels with the book.
Examples: CsvClearedOption
| Setting        | WhatIsImported | WhatTheTransactionIs      |
| On, by default | A CSV file     | Cleared                   |
| Off            | A CSV file     | Uncleared                 |
| Off            | An OFX file    | Cleared, as the file says |
| Either         | Typed in       | Uncleared                 |

Attributes CsvClearedOption
| Attribute            | Type   | Default |
| Setting              | String |         |
| WhatIsImported       | String |         |
| WhatTheTransactionIs | String |         |

Scenario A book that says not to clear leaves a CSV import uncleared
Description The same file as the category scenario above, in a book whose
\ option is off. Nothing else about the import changes -- the rows,
\ the categories and the accounts created are what they were.
Given the book setting is : BookSetting Vertical
| SetClearedOnCsvImport | false |
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type     | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking        | Checking | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries     | Expense  | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense  | false       |
Given the csv profile is : CsvProfile Vertical
| Name           | Quicken Export |
| DateColumn     | Date           |
| PayeeColumn    | Payee          |
| CategoryColumn | Category       |
| AmountStyle    | Signed         |
| AmountColumn   | Amount         |
Given the file contains
"""
Date,Payee,Category,Amount
01/15/2024,Harris Teeter,Expenses:Groceries,-45.00
"""
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When rows imported
Then transactions are : Transaction
| Ref | SourceAccount   | Date       | Payee         | Destination        | Amount | Cleared   |
| T1  | Assets:Checking | 2024-01-15 | Harris Teeter | Expenses:Groceries | -45.00 | Uncleared |

